### Component 3: Backend Production Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [constants.ts](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/davidprz/projects/CaloriesTracker/backend/CaloriesTrackerBackend/nodeApp/constants.ts) & [app.ts](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/davidprz/projects/CaloriesTracker/backend/CaloriesTrackerBackend/nodeApp/app.ts)
- Allow dynamic origins via `CLIENT_ORIGIN` environment variable (e.g. `https://calories-tracker.vercel.app`), while maintaining local `localhost:5173` fallback for development.
- Add `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` for HTTPS reverse proxies (Render, Railway, Nginx).

#### [MODIFY] [Users/routes.ts](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/davidprz/projects/CaloriesTracker/backend/CaloriesTrackerBackend/Users/routes.ts)
- Update `res.cookie('refreshToken', ...)` configuration:
  - In production (`NODE_ENV === 'production'`), set `sameSite: 'none'` and `secure: true` so cross-site cookies between different deployment domains (e.g. Vercel frontend + Render backend) are accepted by modern browsers.
- Add a dedicated `/api/users/demo-login` route that automatically logs in the demo account without password prompts.

